# RP9 §5.4 node authentication (with ER-01: A4 = r_CM * P_CM) in OFMC's AnB language, OUTSIDER-ONLY
# variant: the cluster member, cluster head and base station are honest constants (cm, ch, bs); the
# intruder plays none of them, so it knows no pseudo-identity scalar. Each role knows exactly the
# scalars RP9 gives it; xr is a function nobody publishes.
#   P_CH = exp(g, xr(BS,ch)), A1 = exp(g,Rch), A2 = exp(P_CH, Rch)
#   Enc(m, Pu_i) (Boneh-Franklin IBE, IA-03) -> {m}pk(i)
# The cm checks A2 = (ID_BS xor ID_CH) * A1 by computing exp(A1, xr(bs,ch)).
# Note on the 2-session result: AnB has no receiver-side record of nonces already accepted, shared
# across sessions. Without such a record, replaying an EM1 succeeds; RP9's replay protection rests
# entirely on that record, which RP9 does not specify. The runtime keeps one, so Lab L1 is blocked.

Protocol: RP9_NodeAuthentication_OutsiderOnly

Types: Agent cm,ch,bs;
       Number Nch,Ncm,Rch,Rcm,g;
       Function pk,xr

Knowledge: cm: cm,ch,bs,pk,inv(pk(cm)),g,xr(bs,ch),xr(ch,cm);
           ch: cm,ch,bs,pk,inv(pk(ch)),g,xr(bs,ch),xr(ch,cm);
           bs: cm,ch,bs,pk,inv(pk(bs)),g,xr(bs,ch)


Actions:

ch->cm: {exp(g,Rch), exp(exp(g,xr(bs,ch)),Rch), Nch}pk(cm)
cm->ch: {exp(g,Rcm), exp(exp(g,xr(ch,cm)),Rcm), Ncm}pk(ch)
ch->bs: {exp(g,Rch), exp(exp(g,xr(bs,ch)),Rch), Nch}pk(bs)

Goals:

cm authenticates ch on Nch
ch authenticates cm on Ncm
bs authenticates ch on Nch
